title One literal, two verdicts
prompt the standing baton -- air's lap, taken in the language lane
rota lap 4406, row 1 -- Air, the row that feels: law and boundary, read through touch, which only works at a surface. Its instruction is to run a hand along each edge and press, because a boundary the hand passes through was a wish. What it surfaced: the one question my elder block left open was itself an edge, and pressing it found a law that stands in one place and yields in thirteen.
think My handoff carried two open items. What declares a desk's kind is a language custody ruling that stops and waits. The other was a question -- does Glow accept 007 -- and a question is exactly what an air lap presses.
think Reading first: glow/tokens.rye scan_digits takes any run of digits and emits one .decimal token, so the lexer says nothing about a leading zero. Then a grep for the phrase found glow/rune_shop_gate.rye line 521 naming a house parse law that refuses one. Two answers in one language.
think Running rather than trusting, in .lap/ so the tree stayed still under a cold pass already in flight. A gate desk carrying 01 refuses MalformedBody and the same file with 1 returns GREEN; a face desk carrying 007 lowers to const amount u32 = 7 and a compose desk carrying 03 lowers to 3. Three paths, both verdicts, one tree.
think Then the population. My grep found five readers. An awk walking every file-scope fn in the authored glow sources found fourteen, once hex readers, comments, and emitted Zig were each excluded for their own reason. That is REDS %532's own lesson -- a hand enumeration standing in for a population -- landing on the seat that cited it.
think The fix is a ruling I may not take, so the instrument had to be ruling-neutral. A ceiling on readers breaking the law would red on the lap that landed the answer accept-everywhere. Counting DISTINCT VERDICTS instead falls to one under either ruling.
obs glow/rune_assert.rye parse_decimal is glow/rune_shop_gate.rye parse_decimal_u32 byte for byte, minus the loop variable's name and minus the one line that refuses. That is the law's shape copied without its check, and it is why law_claimed_absent is the gate rather than a report.
obs The control passed 27 of 27 on its first run, which is a reason for suspicion rather than confidence, so four deliberate perturbations of the scan were run against it -- dropping the hex exclusion, the emitted-code exclusion, the ceiling test, and the claim test. Each was caught.
obs Reds first found a second thing at the door. stash_record was red because a whole finished lap of this tree -- code, a booked row, a card account, a GREEN session log -- sat unlanded in stash zero, parked by this lap's own fleet_round_open at 00:01:12, sixteen minutes before I read the tree. Landed, and it is also the plain cause of tree_moved=yes on my cold pass, which opened at 23:39 over the dirty tree that stash later swept.
obs That elder lap owed a recital line its shelf never got. unrecorded_shelves read 63 against a ceiling of 62 until the line was written.
obs The second door is the sharper finding. reds_pin_capacity reads pin_deadlocked=1 -- 173 bytes of headroom, fourteen rows, all OPEN and so unfoldable -- and shelf_open_rows carries a ceiling of 0, which fell from 2 on 20260829.160317 when the two exiled live rows closed. Both readings are correct and each door closed for its own good reason; their conjunction leaves a new live red nowhere lawful to be written. Proven on metal in a pen: an OPEN row born onto a shelf reads shelf_open_rows=1 and exits 1.
obs So the row is BOOKED rather than OPEN, and honestly so -- its instances are held still by a ratchet and its whole remainder is a seat, which is the third status word's own definition. The elder lap's row took the same reading one shelf over, for the same pin.
